    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nOpen mini.files in current file directory with current file selected.  Expanded by cwd\r\n\r\nToday, i have to do it:\r\n```lua\r\nMiniFiles.open(vim.fn.expand(\"%:p:h\"))\r\n```\r\n\r\nBut this have two problems:\r\n\r\n1 - If i run again on same file, it will go to last place it was\r\n2 - i can see the previous folders.\r\n\r\nThe ideal is to open like that:\r\n\r\n(I am on mini.lua buffer and call the command)\r\n![image](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/9551316/dd48af59-8df2-4234-94b1-1cc4b687a0c0)\r\n\r\n\r\nSuggestion:\r\n\r\nMiniFiles.open_in_file(filename)\r\n\r\nor\r\n\r\nMiniFiles.open_in_current_file()",
    "closed_at": "2023-07-10T07:50:40Z",
